<article class="env-lemma" id="00FR">
       
      
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00FR">Lemma <span data-tag="00FR">10.31.6</span>.</a> If $R$ is a Noetherian ring then $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R)$ has finitely many irreducible components. In other words $R$ has finitely many minimal primes. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/00FQ" data-tag="00FQ">10.31.5</a> and Topology, Lemma <a href="/tag/0052" data-tag="0052">5.9.2</a> we see there are finitely many irreducible components. By Lemma <a href="/tag/00ES" data-tag="00ES">10.26.1</a> these correspond to minimal primes of $R$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>